Here is the complete ConfigureAuthenticator.sh solution using your existing PHP-FPM stack—keeping the exact same unified User-Repo Override -> ADT Default -> Syntax Fallback architecture, RAM-backed (/dev/shm) 10-minute self-destructing links, and one-way SSH Reverse Proxy sync.
Keeping PHP on the Authenticator for now means you don't have to rewrite your existing PHP login/mailer logic during your refactor, while still getting all the security and directory-structure upgrades.

